    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Although SPSC members are appointed by the Governor, they can only be removed by the President of India.",
        "Service conditions of UPSC members are framed by the President, whereas for Supreme Court Judges, Parliament determines conditions by law.",
        "Removal of PSC members requires a compulsory reference and inquiry by the Supreme Court under Article 317."
      ],
      "id": "68g4h84"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Chairman and other members of the UPSC are appointed by the President of India.",
        "The service conditions of UPSC members are determined by the President and cannot be varied to their disadvantage after appointment.",
        "A UPSC member holds office for a term of six years or until attaining the age of 65 years, whichever is earlier.",
        "Members of Public Service Commissions are ineligible for re-appointment to the same office to ensure independence and impartiality."
      ],
